Steps:
[NAV] {{BACK_URL}}/ui/graphiql/sales-rep
[WAIT] GraphiQL editor loaded (scoped sales-rep schema)
[AUTH] role=SR_REP_PRIMARY — POST {{BACK_URL}}/connect/token with SR_REP_PRIMARY credentials — MUST include the form param storeId ({{STORE_ID}}; use {{STORE_ID_SECONDARY}} for a rep bound to the secondary store): store-bound rep/buyer accounts return HTTP 400 invalid_grant without it (verified vcptcore-qa 2026-07-16); insert "Authorization: Bearer <token>" in the Headers tab via execCommand('insertText') (graphiql-interaction.md Step 2)
[ACT] (main) open a new tab; click query editor; type:
query {
  salesRepCustomers {
    totalCount
    pageInfo { hasNextPage hasPreviousPage startCursor endCursor }
    items { organizationId organizationName lastOrder { id number createdDate status total { amount formattedAmount currency { code symbol } } itemsCount } }
  }
}
[GQL] (main) execute (Ctrl+Enter)
[READ] (main) response panel via browser_snapshot

Assertions:
[ERRORS] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] data.salesRepCustomers.totalCount >= 4 {DOC}
[DATA] items[] contains organizationId = {{served_org_a}} AND organizationId = {{served_org_b}} {DOC}
[DATA] items[] does NOT contain organizationId = {{not_served_org}} {DOC}

[ERRORS] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] the item with organizationId = @td(ORG_ACME.id) has a non-null lastOrder {DOC}
[DATA] that lastOrder.createdDate is the MOST RECENT among orders SR_REP_PRIMARY (the calling rep) itself placed for ORG_ACME — NOT simply the org's globally most-recent order across all actors; per the finalized 'Last order = My last order' semantic (VCST-5304, 2026-07-16), an order placed for ORG_ACME by a different actor/rep, or an admin-seeded order, must not surface as this rep's lastOrder even if it is newer (corroborated live 2026-07-17 on vcptcore-qa: admin-seeded orders do not appear as lastOrder) {DOC}
[DATA] lastOrder.total.amount > 0 {OBSERVED}
[DATA] lastOrder.total.currency.code is non-empty {OBSERVED}
[DATA] lastOrder.itemsCount > 0 {DOC}

[ERRORS] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] items[] contains organizationId = {{org_active}} {DOC}
[DATA] items[] does NOT contain organizationId = {{org_locked}} {DOC}

[ERRORS] (storeA) errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] (storeA) ORG_ACME's lastOrder.number is the OLDER (storeA) order, NOT the newer storeB order {DOC}
[ERRORS] (storeB) errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] (storeB) ORG_ACME's lastOrder.number is the storeB order {DOC}
[ERRORS] (allStores) errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] (allStores) ORG_ACME's lastOrder.number equals (storeB)'s (globally most recent, across stores) {DOC}
[DATA] both the storeA and storeB orders referenced above are SR_REP_PRIMARY's OWN rep-flow-created orders for ORG_ACME, not another actor's/admin-seeded — lastOrder attribution is scoped to the calling rep first, then filtered by store (VCST-5304 sync, 2026-07-17) {DOC}

[ERRORS] (page1) errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] (page1) pageInfo.hasNextPage = true {DOC}
[COUNT] (page1) items.length = 2 {DOC}
[DATA] (page2) items[] has no organizationName overlap with (page1) items[] {DOC}
[ERRORS] (keyword) errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] (keyword) every items[].organizationName contains the keyword substring {DOC}
[DATA] (desc) items.0.organizationName != (page1) items.0.organizationName (opposite sort direction surfaces a different first item) {DOC}

