[AUTH] role=SR_REP_PRIMARY — POST {{BACK_URL}}/connect/token with SR_REP_PRIMARY credentials — MUST include the form param storeId ({{STORE_ID}}; use {{STORE_ID_SECONDARY}} for a rep bound to the secondary store): store-bound rep/buyer accounts return HTTP 400 invalid_grant without it (verified vcptcore-qa 2026-07-16); insert "Authorization: Bearer <token>" in the Headers tab via execCommand('insertText') (graphiql-interaction.md Step 2)
[ACT] (main) open a new tab; click query editor; type:
query {
  salesRepOrders(organizationId: "{{org}}") {
    totalCount
    pageInfo { hasNextPage hasPreviousPage startCursor endCursor }
    items { id number createdDate status statusDisplayValue total { amount formattedAmount currency { code symbol } } itemsCount organizationId organizationName }
  }
}
[GQL] (main) execute (Ctrl+Enter)
[READ] (main) response panel via browser_snapshot

Assertions:
[ERRORS] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] data.salesRepOrders.totalCount >= 2 {DOC}
[DATA] items.0.createdDate >= items.1.createdDate (newest first, default createdDate:desc) {DOC}
[DATA] items.0.total.amount > 0 {OBSERVED}
[DATA] items.0.total.currency.code is non-empty {OBSERVED}
[DATA] items.0.itemsCount > 0 {DOC}
[DATA] items.0.organizationId = {{org}} {DOC}

[ERRORS] (page1) errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] (page1) pageInfo.hasNextPage = true {DOC}
[COUNT] (page1) items.length = 2 {DOC}
[DATA] (page2) items[] has no number overlap with (page1) items[] {DOC}
[ERRORS] (keyword) errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] (keyword) totalCount narrows to exactly 1 (the seeded Beacon order) and that item's number contains "SRO-ACME-KEYWORD" — {{ORDER_KEYWORD_TOKEN}} ('Beacon') matches the order's INDEXED CustomerName; NOTE the response organizationName field returns the denormalized ORGANIZATION name (not the order's raw CustomerName), so assert on the narrowing + number, not on the organizationName value (verified vcptcore-qa 2026-07-16; item field is organizationName, not customerName — mini-verify 2026-07-17) {DOC}

[ERRORS] (storeA) errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] (storeA) items[] excludes the {{STORE_ID_SECONDARY}} order even though it is newer {DOC}
[ERRORS] (allStores) errors[] empty {DOC}
[COUNT] (allStores) items.length > (storeA) items.length {DOC}

[ERRORS] (filter) errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] (filter) every items[].status = "Cancelled" (default SalesRepOrderStatusService maps each store Order.Status value 1:1; option name == raw status) {DOC}
[DATA] (filter) no items[].status = "New" or "Processing" {DOC}
[DATA] (filter) totalCount equals the count of (baseline) items with status "Cancelled" {DOC}

[ERRORS] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] items[] includes at least one status = "New" AND at least one status = "Cancelled" {DOC}
[DATA] no items[].status = "Processing" (excluded — union of the two selected raw statuses only) {DOC}

[ERRORS] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] for the Cancelled order, items[].status = "Cancelled" (raw status preserved, not localized) {DOC}
[DATA] for that same order, items[].statusDisplayValue is non-empty and reflects the {{culture}} localization (differs from a raw enum dump, or matches the store's configured localized label) {DOC}

[ERRORS] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] items[] includes an entry with organizationId = {{org_a}} AND an entry with organizationId = {{org_b}} {OBSERVED}
[DATA] items[] does NOT include any entry with organizationId = {{unassigned_org}} (unassigned org excluded from the dashboard) {OBSERVED}
[DATA] every items[].organizationName is non-empty (denormalized name or member-lookup fallback) {OBSERVED}

[ERRORS] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] data.salesRepOrderStatuses is non-empty {DOC}
[DATA] items include name = "New" {DOC}
[DATA] every items[] entry has a non-blank localizedName (label localized per {{culture}}; default SalesRepOrderStatusService exposes each store Order.Status value 1:1, name == raw status — a composite grouped option is a project override, see SR-GQL-028) {DOC}
[DATA] "New"'s name is a value valid as input to salesRepOrders(statuses:[...]) per SR-GQL-030 {DOC}

[ERRORS] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] data.salesRepCustomers.totalCount >= 1 (the X-API still returns the rep's data — membership scoping is the only gate, per README §Settings) {DOC}
[DATA] items[] still contains organizationId = {{org}} {DOC}

[ERRORS] errors[] empty {DOC}
[DATA] data.salesRepCustomer.address.line1 = @td(ORG_ACME.line1) {DOC}
[DATA] data.salesRepCustomer.address.city = @td(ORG_ACME.city) {DOC}
[DATA] data.salesRepCustomer.address.regionName = @td(ORG_ACME.regionName) {DOC}
[DATA] data.salesRepCustomer.address.postalCode = @td(ORG_ACME.postalCode) {DOC}
[DATA] data.salesRepCustomer.address.countryCode = @td(ORG_ACME.countryCode) {DOC}
[DATA] the iconUrl key is present in the response shape (either null or a non-empty URL string, not omitted) — no fixture org in this dataset has an uploaded logo, so a non-null value is not asserted here {DOC}

[ERRORS] errors[] empty {OBSERVED}
